        MCP server for personal productivity experiments, without affecting any
        teammate's configuration or committing anything to the shared repo.
A) Add it to the project's `.mcp.json` temporarily, and remember to remove it before
   committing.
B) Add it to their personal `~/.claude.json`, which keeps it available only to them
   without touching shared, version-controlled configuration.
C) Add it as a new custom MCP tool description inside `CLAUDE.md`.
D) Request that the whole team install it via `.mcp.json` first, then experiment with it
   once it's shared.

**B14-Q3.** A shared MCP server in `.mcp.json` requires a per-developer API token, and
        the team wants the config file itself to be safely committed to version
        control without leaking anyone's actual token value.
A) Commit the file with one team member's token hardcoded, and have everyone else use
