B) Use `${ENV_VAR}` expansion syntax in `.mcp.json` (e.g., `${DEPLOY_API_TOKEN}`) so the
   committed file references an environment variable name, and each developer supplies
   their own actual token value locally, outside version control.
C) Leave the server out of `.mcp.json` entirely and have each developer configure it
   manually, from memory, every time they set up a new machine.
D) Store the token directly in the MCP server's source code, since environment variables
   aren't supported.

